## 4. Third-party material

`scripts/wi.py` — the deterministic core — has **no dependencies**. It is
standard-library-only Python and is tested to run air-gapped on Python 3.8. That
is not a convenience claim; it is the reason the deterministic tier is worth
anything, because a tier whose value is *you have to trust nothing* cannot have
a supply chain.

`services/api/` is the optional TypeScript reference runtime and does carry
Node dependencies. Its dependency licenses are those declared by the packages in
`services/api/package-lock.json`. It is not required to run the tool, verify a
release, or open a proof capsule.

## 5. Verification

The offline verification path — a stranger checking a proof capsule with no
model, no network and no account — is deliberately unencumbered. If any patent
right described in `PATENTS.md` is ever granted and asserted, it will not be
asserted against verification of an artifact this project produced. A proof a
stranger cannot verify is not a proof, and a licensing term that makes
verification risky would destroy the thing being protected.

